--- A3 interpretive question ---
Is there any prior in this grid under which PP.H4 exceeds PP.H1?
ANSWER: Yes, but only under priors more permissive than the default.
        Along the p12 axis (p1=p2=1e-04 fixed), PP.H4 first exceeds PP.H1 at
        p12 = 5e-05, i.e. 5x the default; at the default p12 = 1e-05,
        PP.H1 = 0.536 still exceeds PP.H4 = 0.447.
        Along the p1=p2 axis (p12=1e-05 fixed), lowering p1=p2 to 1e-05 also
        flips the ordering (PP.H4 = 0.893), but that sets p12 equal to p1.
        Every cell in which PP.H4 exceeds PP.H1 has p12 >= 1e-05.
