   more than 8-fold above the conventional threshold of 10.
2. Does Q_A become significant (p < 0.05) anywhere in the plausible range?
   ANSWER: No -- Q_A ranges 6.277 to 6.285 on 7 df (p = 0.507 to 0.508), null throughout.
3. Do the MVMR-IVW point estimates move at all?
   ANSWER: No -- identical to 8 significant figures at every rho (confirmed).
   This is invariance by construction, not an empirical finding: MVMR 0.4.6's
   ivw_mvmr() accepts gencov but never uses it -- it warns when gencov == 0 and
   then fits lm(betaYG ~ -1 + betaX1 + betaX2, weights = 1/seBetaYG^2).
   gencov enters only strength_mvmr() and pleiotropy_mvmr().

   Direction note: the biologically expected sign of rho is negative
   (transferrin rises in iron deficiency). Negative rho RAISES conditional F
   (669.99 / 126.02 at rho = -0.6 vs 278.20 / 93.88 at rho = 0), so setting the
   covariance to zero was the conservative choice for instrument strength.

